<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="An educational DFA simulation where you choose a keyword and scan campus messages for it.">
  <title>Emergency Keyword Detection | DFA Simulator</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="app-shell">
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> THEORY OF COMPUTATION · REAL-LIFE APPLICATION</div>
        <h1>Emergency Help<br><span>Detection System</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-subtitle">A campus safety desk receives messages from students. Enter any keyword you want, and this DFA scans each message one character at a time to find it.</p>
        <div class="hero-tags"><span>◉ Deterministic Finite Automaton</span><span>↳ Keyword: <strong id="heroKeywordTag">HELP</strong></span><span>⚡ Step-by-step scan</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="radar-ring ring-one"></div><div class="radar-ring ring-two"></div><div class="radar-ring ring-three"></div>
        <div class="shield-mark">✓</div><div class="radar-blip blip-one"></div><div class="radar-blip blip-two"></div>
        <div class="hero-visual-label">DFA ACTIVE <span></span></div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="scenario-section">
        <div class="section-intro">
          <div><span class="step-label">REAL-LIFE SCENARIO</span><h2>Message from a student</h2></div>
          <p>Choose a sample message, or type your own message and keyword below.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="scenario-grid">
          <button class="scenario-card selected" type="button" data-scenario="library">
            <span class="scenario-icon icon-red">✚</span><span class="scenario-text"><strong>Library Emergency</strong><small>Help request near library</small></span><span class="scenario-arrow">↗</span>
          </button>
          <button class="scenario-card" type="button" data-scenario="gate">
            <span class="scenario-icon icon-red">✚</span><span class="scenario-text"><strong>Main Gate Alert</strong><small>Help request at main gate</small></span><span class="scenario-arrow">↗</span>
          </button>
          <button class="scenario-card" type="button" data-scenario="hostel">
            <span class="scenario-icon icon-red">✚</span><span class="scenario-text"><strong>Hostel Emergency</strong><small>Help request near hostel</small></span><span class="scenario-arrow">↗</span>
          </button>
          <button class="scenario-card" type="button" data-scenario="noMatch">
            <span class="scenario-icon icon-blue">⌕</span><span class="scenario-text"><strong>Test No Match</strong><small>Message without the default keyword</small></span><span class="scenario-arrow">↗</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel input-panel">
        <div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="step-label">01 / INPUT</span><h2>Student emergency message</h2></div><span class="live-chip"><span></span> SIMULATION</span></div>
        <div class="input-grid">
          <label class="field message-field">Message received by campus safety desk
            <textarea id="textInput" rows="3" maxlength="500" placeholder="Type or paste a message..."></textarea>
            <small>The message is scanned from left to right. Matching ignores letter case.</small>
          </label>
          <label class="field keyword-field">Keyword to find (editable)
            <input id="patternInput" type="text" maxlength="24" value="HELP" aria-label="Type the keyword to detect" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
            <small>Type any word (for example: HELP, FIRE, SOS, DANGER), then click “Build DFA &amp; Scan”. Matching ignores letter case.</small>
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="actions-row">
          <button id="buildBtn" class="btn btn-primary" type="button"><span>⚙</span> Build DFA &amp; Scan</button>
          <button id="exampleBtn" class="btn btn-ghost" type="button">↻ Restore selected sample</button>
          <span id="error" class="error-message" role="alert"></span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel automaton-panel">
        <div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="step-label">02 / MODEL</span><h2 id="modelTitle">DFA for the keyword HELP</h2><p id="modelDescription" class="section-note">q0 = no match; each next state represents one more character matched.</p></div><div class="state-legend"><span><i class="legend-start"></i> Start state</span><span><i class="legend-accept"></i> Accept state</span></div></div>
        <div id="automaton" class="automaton-viewport" aria-label="Finite automaton state diagram"></div>
        <div class="automaton-footnote"><span class="info-dot">i</span> <span id="automatonHint">A matching character advances the DFA. Reaching the accepting state means the complete keyword was found.</span></div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel table-panel">
        <div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="step-label">03 / TRANSITIONS</span><h2>Transition table</h2><p class="section-note">δ(state, character) tells the DFA which state to enter next.</p></div></div>
        <div id="tableWrap" class="table-viewport"></div>
        <p id="tableHint" class="table-hint">“Other” means any character not in the keyword alphabet; it transitions to q0.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel simulation-panel">
        <div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="step-label">04 / LIVE SIMULATION</span><h2>Scan the message</h2><p class="section-note">Advance one character at a time or let the DFA run automatically.</p></div><div id="status" class="status-chip">READY TO SCAN</div></div>
        <div class="message-label-row"><span>MESSAGE STREAM</span><span id="scanPercent">0% scanned</span></div>
        <div id="textDisplay" class="text-display" aria-label="Message characters"></div>
        <div class="progress-track"><div id="progressBar" class="progress-bar"></div></div>
        <div class="sim-info-grid">
          <div class="sim-info"><span class="info-label">Next character</span><strong id="currentChar">—</strong><small id="characterHint">Waiting for input</small></div>
          <div class="sim-info"><span class="info-label">Current state</span><strong id="currentState">q0</strong><small>State before next transition</small></div>
          <div class="sim-info"><span class="info-label">Predicted next state</span><strong id="nextState">q1</strong><small>Based on transition function</small></div>
          <div class="sim-info"><span class="info-label">Characters processed</span><strong id="position">0 / 0</strong><small>Read from left to right</small></div>
        </div>
        <div id="message" class="event-message" role="status" aria-live="polite"><span class="event-symbol">ⓘ</span><span>Build the DFA, then press Next Step or Play to scan the message.</span></div>
        <div class="simulation-controls">
          <button id="prevBtn" class="btn btn-ghost" type="button">← Previous</button>
          <button id="nextBtn" class="btn btn-primary" type="button">Next Step →</button>
          <button id="playBtn" class="btn btn-play" type="button">▶ Play</button>
          <button id="resetBtn" class="btn btn-ghost" type="button">↺ Reset</button>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="bottom-grid">
        <div class="panel results-panel">
          <div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="step-label">05 / RESULT</span><h2>Detection report</h2></div></div>
          <div class="metrics-grid">
            <div class="metric"><span>Keyword detections</span><strong id="matchCount">0</strong><small>Matches found so far</small></div>
            <div class="metric"><span>Transitions completed</span><strong id="transitionCount">0</strong><small>Characters processed</small></div>
            <div class="metric"><span>Keyword length</span><strong id="patternLength">4</strong><small>Number of characters</small></div>
          </div>
          <div class="matches-heading">Detection positions <span>1-based indexing</span></div>
          <div id="matches" class="matches-list">No keyword detected yet.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="panel explanation-panel">
          <span class="step-label">REAL-WORLD CONNECTION</span><h2>How the emergency alert check works</h2>
          <div class="workflow">
            <div class="workflow-step"><span>1</span><div><strong>Receive</strong><p>A student sends a message to the campus safety desk.</p></div></div>
            <div class="workflow-step"><span>2</span><div><strong>Check for the keyword</strong><p>The DFA reads one character at a time. Each state represents how much of your chosen keyword has matched so far.</p></div></div>
            <div class="workflow-step"><span>3</span><div><strong>Flag a match</strong><p>If the accepting state is reached, the simulation highlights your keyword and shows its position in the message.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="safety-note"><strong>Important limitation</strong><p>Educational prototype only: it checks for the exact characters in your keyword, not the meaning of a message. It is not connected to campus security or real emergency services.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer><span class="footer-mark">TC</span><span>Theory of Computation · Custom Keyword Detection with DFA</span><span></span></footer>
  </div>
  <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
